/* ===== LAO LANGUAGE PACK (Zones 1–10) =====
   Lao-DRIVEN curriculum, researched before shipping (Wikipedia Lao script/
   grammar, Wikivoyage Lao phrasebook, Omniglot, Preply Lao word/family lists).
   Romanization scheme (ASCII only, enforced — NO Lao script in rom fields):
   - Spoken Lao, no tone marks written (tones are taught inside real words,
     never in isolation — Lao has 6 tones; exaggerate + let the audio lead).
   - Consonants: k (ກ), kh (ຂ ຄ), ng (ງ), j (ຈ), s (ສ ຊ), ny (ຍ), d (ດ),
     t (ຕ), th (ຖ ທ), n (ນ), b (ບ), p (ປ), ph (ຜ ພ — a hard aspirated p,
     NOT an f), f (ຝ ຟ), m (ມ), y (ຢ), l (ລ), v (ວ), h (ຫ ຮ), r (ຣ, rare);
     ອ is a silent glottal vowel-carrier. Aspirated = written with h (kh/th/ph).
   - The 27 consonants fall into THREE tone classes (high/middle/low) that set
     a syllable's tone — Lao's answer to Khmer's two series. Taught by ear.
   - Vowels: a/aa (ະ າ), i/ii (ິ ີ), eu (ຶ ື), u/uu (ຸ ູ), e (ເະ ເ),
     ae (ແະ ແ), o (ົ ໂ), aw (ໍ /ɔ/), ai (ໄ ໃ), ao (ເົາ), am (ຳ), ua (ົວ),
     ia (ຽ ເັຍ), eua (ເືອ). Long vowels doubled where it helps (aa, ii, uu).
   - Words romanized as pronounced: sabaidee, khop jai, khoi, jao, khao, nam.
   Lao has no verb conjugation, no gender, no plurals (lean on the freebies);
   word order is SVO; tense/aspect ride on particles (ແລ້ວ past, ຈະ/ຊິ future,
   ກຳລັງ progressive, ບໍ່ negation); to-be splits ແມ່ນ (identity) vs ຢູ່
   (location); counting is noun + number + classifier. Real Lao often writes
   no spaces between words — word-builder tiles are teaching aids.
   Content quality is research-verified, not native-reviewed (see CLAUDE.md).
   Art: secular Laos — Mekong river at dusk, limestone karsts, wooden stilt
   house, longtail boat, river reeds. Mascot: baby water buffalo. */

